---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LegalPage from "../../components/LegalPage.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | World of Alphabets" canonicalPath="/alphabets/privacy">
  <LegalPage eyebrow="World of Alphabets" themeColor="app-alphabets">
    <h1>Privacy Policy for World of Alphabets</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> May 6, 2026</p>

    <p>
      This privacy policy applies to the World of Alphabets app (the &quot;Application&quot;) for mobile devices,
      provided by Khonsu Development (the &quot;Service Provider&quot;). The Application is supported by ads and is
      provided &quot;AS IS&quot;.
    </p>

    <h2>What information does the Application process and why?</h2>
    <h3>Information you provide</h3>
    <p>
      The Application does not require you to create an account. If you contact the Service Provider (for example, by
      email), the Service Provider will process the information you provide in your message to respond to you.
    </p>

    <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
    <p>
      The Application and its third-party service providers may process certain technical information automatically,
      such as device information (for example, device model, operating system version), IP address, app version,
      approximate location inferred from IP address, and identifiers associated with your device or app instance (for
      example, the advertising ID). This information is used to deliver ads, measure ad performance, improve stability,
      and diagnose crashes.
    </p>

    <h2>Does the Application collect precise real-time location?</h2>
    <p>The Application does not collect precise real-time location information (for example, GPS location).</p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>The Application uses third-party services that have their own privacy policies. In particular:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">Google AdMob</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy">Firebase Crashlytics</a>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Legal bases (EEA/UK)</h2>
    <p>
      If you are located in the EEA or the UK, the Service Provider processes personal data under the following legal
      bases, depending on the purpose:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Consent</strong>: for ad-related identifiers and similar technologies where required, via Google&apos;s
        User Messaging Platform (UMP).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legitimate interests</strong>: to ensure security, prevent abuse, and diagnose and fix crashes (for
        example, via Crashlytics).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal obligations</strong>: where processing is required to comply with applicable laws.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Consent management and opt-out</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Manage consent (EEA/UK)</strong>: if you are shown a consent prompt, you can typically review and update
        your choices in the Application&apos;s privacy settings (for example, a &quot;Manage consent&quot; option) where
        available.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Device controls</strong>: you can limit ad personalization via your device settings (for example,
        Android advertising settings).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Uninstall</strong>: you can stop further data processing by uninstalling the Application.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      The Service Provider does not typically receive crash and ad measurement data directly on their own servers. This
      information is processed by the third-party services listed above and retained according to their retention
      settings and policies. The Service Provider retains communications (if you contact them) for as long as needed to
      respond and for a reasonable period thereafter.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The Application is not intended for children and the Service Provider does not knowingly collect personal data
      from children. If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child has provided personal information, contact
      the Service Provider at{" "}
      <a href="mailto:khonsu.development@gmail.com"> khonsu.development@gmail.com. </a>
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      The Service Provider takes reasonable measures to protect information processed in connection with the
      Application. However, no method of transmission or storage is completely secure.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights such as access, rectification, deletion, objection, restriction,
      and portability. If the GDPR (or UK GDPR) applies, you also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory
      authority. To exercise your rights, contact{" "}
      <a href="mailto:khonsu.development@gmail.com"> khonsu.development@gmail.com. </a>
    </p>

    <h2>International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      The third-party services used by the Application may process data on servers located in different countries. Where
      required, transfers are protected using appropriate safeguards, such as standard contractual clauses.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time. The Service Provider will publish the updated policy on this
      page and update the &quot;Last updated&quot; date.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about privacy while using the Application, contact the Service Provider at{" "}
      <a href="mailto:khonsu.development@gmail.com"> khonsu.development@gmail.com. </a>
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</BaseLayout>
